{
  "info": {
    "name": "11 \u00b7 Organizations & tenancy",
    "description": "Tenancy root \u2014 the admin-managed organization resource and its membership, plus the delete guard that keeps referenced orgs alive.\n\n**Flow.** A) org CRUD (create/get/list-filter/rename, name-collision 409, missing 404); B) members (assign/list/remove, non-member 404); C) the tenancy invariant \u2014 an `organization`-access-level group references the org, so deleting the org is **blocked (409)** until the group is freed (switched to `public` with `organization_id` cleared), then it deletes (204); D) RBAC negatives \u2014 `viewer` (non-admin) reads (200) but is denied create/update/delete/manage-members (403), and a no-token request is 401.\n\n**Auth model.** Per-request (not collection-level): `{{admin_token}}` for management, `{{viewer_token}}` for the non-admin negatives, `noauth` for the 401. Setup logs in both seeded identities \u2014 **self-contained, no `00-bootstrap` and no manual verification-token step** (the non-admin is the seeded `viewer`, not a fresh registration).\n\n**Permissions.** `organizations:read` is held by every role; `create`/`update`/`delete`/`manage_members` are admin-only.\n\n**Leftovers.** Evaluation groups have no DELETE endpoint, so the folder-C group is left behind (`run_suffix` keeps it unique); Teardown removes org2 (org1 is deleted in folder C).\n\n**Verified:** 30/30 against a live stack (`make up` + `make seedlocal`).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "noauth"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:8000",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "run_suffix",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "admin_token",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "viewer_email",
      "value": "viewer@test.com",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "viewer_password",
      "value": "password123",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "viewer_token",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "member_user_id",
